= Biological computation (simple) =

'''Biological computation''' means that living cells or biological molecules can process information in ways that help them respond to their surroundings or perform engineered tasks.

For example, scientists have built genetic circuits inside bacteria that act somewhat like switches or oscillators. These circuits use molecules and gene activity rather than electronic transistors.

That does not mean a bacterium is just a laptop made of cells. Its chemistry, metabolism, growth, repair and environment matter to everything it does.

